questions.a:
Scenario: RTO road tax calculator for Delhi.
- Vehicle type: Two-wheeler (T) or Four-wheeler (F)
- Fuel type: Petrol (P), Diesel (D), Electric (E)
- Ownership: Individual (I) or Commercial (C)
Tax rules:
1. If Two-wheeler:
   - If Electric: ₹0 (exempt)
   - Else if Petrol: ₹500 (Individual), ₹1000 (Commercial)
   - Else Diesel: ₹700 (Individual), ₹1500 (Commercial)
2. If Four-wheeler:
   - If Electric: ₹0 (exempt)
   - Else if Petrol: ₹3000 (Individual), ₹6000 (Commercial)
   - Else Diesel: ₹5000 (Individual), ₹10000 (Commercial)

Code skeleton (student must fill all branches):
```python
vtype = input("Vehicle (T/F): ").upper()
fuel = input("Fuel (P/D/E): ").upper()
owner = input("Owner (I/C): ").upper()
if vtype == "T":
    if fuel == "E":
        tax = 0
    elif fuel == "P":
        if owner == "I":
            tax = 500
        else:
            tax = 1000
    else:  # Diesel
        if owner == "I":
            tax = 700
        else:
            tax = 1500
elif vtype == "F":
    if fuel == "E":
        tax = 0
    elif fuel == "P":
        if owner == "I":
            tax = 3000
        else:
            tax = 6000
    else:  # Diesel
        if owner == "I":
            tax = 5000
        else:
            tax = 10000
else:
    tax = -1
print("Road Tax:", tax if tax != -1 else "Invalid input")
```
A poor answer uses flat `if-elif` chains without nesting, revealing the student cannot identify hierarchical decision factors.
